{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3780","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3780","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3780\",\"parent_revision\":\"e644bdaab4185525bf56ca5a7e260c265dd60de6\",\"root_revision\":\"56a9da4cb65fd42e430f980a9045bcaf61d93f51919b3f1d7d043fc06f76b1bb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe repository fast test suite passes but emits 144 warnings. Observed categories include MCP logging deprecations, Typer option deprecations, and PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning from dh_paths hanging-stub threads leaking into later dispatch-schema tests. Warning output obscures regressions and contradicts the repository validation policy that warnings should be resolved or explicitly scoped.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:48:59.457994Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: The full fast suite passes while emitting 144 warnings in three categories.\\nevidence: Bounded `uv run pytest` completed with `6591 passed, 54 skipped, 10 xfailed, 144 warnings`; summary grouped 44 MCPDeprecationWarning, 96 Typer DeprecationWarning, and 4 PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning emissions.\\nsource: local bounded reproduction on 2026-09-21.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: FastMCP client logging emits a deprecation under the installed 4.0.2 behavior.\\nevidence: Warning-as-error reproduction failed at `server.py:2609` -> `ctx.info` -> `fastmcp/server/context.py:1357` with `MCPDeprecationWarning: The logging capability is deprecated as of 2026-07-28 (SEP-2577)`. FastMCP 4.0.0 documents support for the 2026-07-28 protocol and deprecation/removal of server push-era capabilities.\\nsource: https://gofastmcp.com/changelog.md and installed FastMCP 4.0.2 runtime traceback.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Typer 0.27.0 warns whenever `is_flag` or `flag_value` is non-None.\\nevidence: Upstream `OptionInfo.__init__` explicitly calls `warnings.warn` when either value is non-None; local source passes `is_flag=True` four times, and warning-as-error produces seven deterministic test failures in one affected file.\\nsource: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fastapi/typer/0.27.0/typer/models.py and https://typer.tiangolo.com/reference/parameters/.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Hanging-stub daemon threads escape their owning tests and raise in later tests.\\nevidence: The red-capable sequence failed later in `TestDispatchSpawn::test_spawn_end_to_end_single_wave` with an ExceptionGroup containing four `PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning` instances; every traceback ends at `test_dh_paths.py:337` after `dh_paths.py:122`.\\nsource: local warning-as-error reproduction on 2026-09-21.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:47:09.598875Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: Eliminate full test suite warning output\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\nGoal: Remove every observed warning from the fast test suite by correcting each emitting code or test lifecycle.\\nConditions:\\n1. Warning categories and counts are reproducible | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Current FastMCP logging behavior is verified from primary upstream/runtime sources | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Current Typer option behavior is verified from primary upstream sources | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Thread-warning trigger and ownership are identified | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Affected systems and deterministic validation commands are known | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:49:50.583400Z</sub>\\n\\nType: recurring-pattern\\nRationale: Three independent obsolete or unmanaged lifecycle patterns produce the same validation failure class, and each repeats across multiple calls/tests.\\nAnalysis Method: 6-sigma category measurement plus evidence-chain root-cause analysis.\\nScenario Target: fast suite passes with 144 warnings -> fast suite passes with zero warnings and category-specific warning-as-error checks pass.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:54:01.278772Z</sub>\\n\\n- Validation logs contain 144 non-actionable warnings despite a passing suite.\\n- Deprecated FastMCP and Typer calls are on removal paths and can become hard failures on upgrades.\\n- Escaped test threads violate test isolation and assign failures to unrelated later tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:48:06.198918Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: 13 files across MCP runtime/tests, migration CLIs/tests, and path-resolution tests.\\n\\n### Code - Producers (write the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` - 15 `ctx.info`/`ctx.warning` calls invoke deprecated MCP client logging.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` - three boolean options explicitly pass unsupported `is_flag=True`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/verify_migration_fidelity.py` - one boolean option explicitly passes unsupported `is_flag=True`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_paths.py` - timeout worker intentionally leaves unexpected exceptions to thread reporting; production behavior is valid, but tests must not leave their synthetic workers to raise after teardown.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` - asserts deprecated context logging and tool behavior.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_groom_sections.py` - exercises groom paths that emit context logging.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_frontend_parity_ops.py` - exercises logging-emitting MCP operations.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` - exercises logging-emitting sync scenarios.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_validator_escape_classification.py` - exercises logging-emitting pull/sync paths.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` - invokes the affected Typer CLI.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_verify_migration_fidelity.py` - invokes the affected Typer CLI.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths.py` - owns the delayed `_hang` stub and its cleanup lifecycle.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` - deterministic downstream collection point used by the thread-warning reproduction; no source change expected.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\nNone identified; user-visible CLI behavior is unchanged.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- `pyproject.toml` - strict warning behavior and dependency versions are validation context; no suppression or downgrade change permitted.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n1. Backlog MCP tool progress reporting -> FastMCP Context -> deprecated MCP logging capability.\\n2. MCP server tests -> in-memory FastMCP client -> warning collection.\\n3. Backlog migration CLI -> Typer option metadata -> CLI parser construction.\\n4. Migration fidelity CLI -> Typer option metadata -> CLI parser construction.\\n5. Migration CLI tests -> Typer runner -> repeated warning emission.\\n6. Git project-root timeout -> daemon worker thread -> queue handoff.\\n7. Hanging-path tests -> delayed synthetic exception -> pytest threadexception hook.\\n8. Dispatch tests -> later test activity long enough to collect escaped thread exceptions.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every listed producer corrected or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected consumer test updated\\n- [ ] No warning filters or dependency downgrades added\\n- [ ] CLI semantics retained\\n- [ ] Full bounded fast suite reports zero warnings\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:53:11.389696Z</sub>\\n\\nPriority: P2\\nEffort: MEDIUM\\nRationale: The suite passes, so delivery is not blocked, but warning volume masks future regressions and all warnings violate the repository validation policy. Scope spans three independent corrections and their focused tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:51:33.212202Z</sub>\\n\\nMISSION_ALIGNED\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\nThe change supports the repository validation policy in `docs/testing.md`: warnings fail validation unless a versioned, scope-limited exception is recorded. Removing deprecated API usage and ensuring test-owned cleanup also follows `ARCHITECTURE.md` acceptance-criterion guidance that verification must be machine-runnable, and `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` keeps MCP wrappers thin around operations. No architecture boundary change is required.\\n\\nConstraint: preserve business-operation output and provider boundaries; replace only deprecated transport-side progress behavior. Preserve `dh_paths.py` production policy of exposing unexpected worker exceptions; repair synthetic test lifecycle instead.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:52:24.793454Z</sub>\\n\\nDeterministic on Python 3.13.15, pytest 9.1.1, FastMCP 4.0.2, Typer 0.27.0.\\n\\n- Full bounded suite: `uv run --script scripts/run_bounded.py --timeout-seconds 600 -- uv run pytest -m \\\"not e2e and not cross_backend and not integration and not research_vault and not slow\\\"` -> PASS with 144 warnings.\\n- FastMCP red check: `uv run pytest -n 0 --no-cov -W error::mcp.shared.exceptions.MCPDeprecationWarning plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py::test_backlog_sync_success_returns_counts` -> FAIL at `ctx.info`.\\n- Typer red check: `uv run pytest -n 0 --no-cov -W error::DeprecationWarning plugins/development-harness/tests/test_migrate_backlog_to_yaml.py` -> 7 failed, 6 passed.\\n- Thread red check: `uv run pytest -n 0 --no-cov -W error::pytest.PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dh_paths.py::TestGitCommonRootHangProtection plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_state.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` -> 1 failed, 73 passed with four delayed `_hang` exceptions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed while validating #3778\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T03:50:42.000019Z</sub>\\n\\n**Measured categories**: FastMCP logging 44, Typer options 96, escaped thread exceptions 4.\\n\\n**Root cause**: Validation dependencies advanced across explicit deprecation/lifecycle boundaries while repository call sites and test doubles retained obsolete assumptions.\\n\\n1. FastMCP: backlog MCP wrappers use Context client-log methods for progress; FastMCP 4.0.2 routes those calls through the protocol logging capability, which warns under the 2026-07-28 protocol.\\n2. Typer: two migration CLIs explicitly set `is_flag=True`; Typer 0.27.0 infers boolean flags and warns on either explicit `is_flag` or `flag_value`.\\n3. Threads: timeout tests create daemon workers whose synthetic `_hang` sleeps beyond the assertion and then raises after monkeypatch teardown; pytest collects those unowned exceptions during later tests.\\n\\n**Systemic correction**: remove obsolete API arguments/calls and make every synthetic worker test-owned through deterministic release and cleanup. Preserve operation result messages, boolean CLI semantics, timeout behavior, and unexpected production exception reporting.\\n\\n**Ruled out**:\\n- Warning filters or pytest configuration changes: hide the failure and violate repository policy.\\n- Dependency downgrade/pin: retains obsolete behavior and defers breakage.\\n- Catching all production thread exceptions: masks genuine GitPython/wrapper defects that `dh_paths.py` intentionally exposes.\\n- Changing dispatch tests: they only reveal a worker escaped from `test_dh_paths.py`; they do not own the defect.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d1fb64ca8fe7324571160de67545ba36bb0dcb45913001f8f43499eb086c030e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVwjFTQ\"}"}